 			<p>“Certainly. Go, dear; I forget that you have any home but this,” and <abbr epub:type="z3998:name-title">Mrs.</abbr> March pressed the white hand that wore the wedding-ring, as if asking pardon for her maternal covetousness.</p>
 			<p>“I shouldn’t have come over if I could have helped it; but I can’t get on without my little woman any more than a⁠—”</p>
 			<p>“Weathercock can without wind,” suggested Jo, as he paused for a simile; Jo had grown quite her own saucy self again since Teddy came home.</p>
